So the shared normalization composes fine with my unwrap. These are edge cases anyway (0 in test).

One more thing in the loop shared part: `ctx["expected"] = _clip_debug(in_outs['outputs'][index])` is set BEFORE my unwrap — fine for logging (shows raw).

Also `ctx["inputs"] = _clip_debug(inputs)` fine.

Now about `args = list(inputs)` — shallow copy, fine. But note the shared dict normalization mutated `inputs` when first arg is dict: `inputs = [{int(k): v ...}]` — replaces the whole args list with single dict arg. That's canonical (weird but upstream). Keep.

